<h3>General Rules<o:p></o:p></h3>

<h3>Overview<o:p></o:p></h3>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>As Bloodhorde, we pride ourselves
on having a group of mature players that are here to have fun and help
eachother. These rules are not meant to be restrictive. Rather, they are here
to let everyone know what our guidelines are, and hopefully make Bloodhorde a
fun group to be with. <o:p></o:p></p>

<h3>General Rules<o:p></o:p></h3>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><u>Bloodhorde is a roleplay
     guild</u>. We ask all members to remain in character when speaking out
     loud in /say and in guild chat. We also ask that members have /roleplay
     (makes you anonymous, except for your guild tag) turned on at at all
     times. We feel this adds to the atmosphere of role play in the sense that
     it prevents you from judging somebody by their level. There are situations
     where you may need to take /roleplay off (raids, LFG, etc) and thats fine,
     but you should turn it back on as soon as you can. We encourage members to
     roleplay their character. We encourage members to think of stories for
     their characters and have fun. If something out of character must be said
     out loud or in guild chat, it should be preceeded by &lt;ooc&gt;. Also try
     to refrain from refering to alts out loud. We are just trying to foster a
     good role play environment for our members to have fun. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><u>Never question autority or
     guild policies in public or in guild chat.</u> We have set up rules to
     help members understand who we are, and what we expect. Bloodhorde members
     are required to know these rules. Questioning authority or guild policies
     in public is considered an act of insurrection and will not be tolerated.
     However, we are not closed to member suggestions. If you have an issue
     with a guild policy or an order/decision by a ranking member, you are
     welcome to contact a ranking member and discuss the issue <b>in private</b>.
     <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><u>Always follow the order of
     command</u>. The ranking members are not here to order members around.
     However, if they feel you are out of line or not following guild policies,
     they may give you an order to correct the sitution. This order is to be
     respected. If you have an issue with the order, follow it, refer to the rule
     above, and talk to them in private. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><u>Fellow Guild members will
     be treated with respect at all times.</u> We pride ourselves as being a
     fun and mature group. Treating fellow members with respect is the
     foundation for a good guild. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><u>No personal arguments in
     guild chat</u>. All arguments are to be resolved through private tells.
     Personal arguments in guild chat are annoying and damages morale. For more
     information, see <a
     href="inner.htm">Inner-Guild
     Dispute Procedures</a>. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><u>Begging will not tolerated</u>.
     Period. Bloodhorde does not owe items or money to anybody. Begging damages
     morale, annoys people, and makes us look bad. Begging includes repeatedly
     asking for free money or items, especially items that are obviously beyond
     your level. Begging also includes repeatedly asking for help getting power
     leveled, camping a creature, or completing a quest that is far beyond your
     level. Bloodhorde is here to help our members, but not to the point of
     doing work for individuals. If someone offers to help in some way, that's
     great, but don't go begging for it. If you are caught begging from either
     Bloodhorde members, or anybody outside Bloodhorde, you will be disbanded
     from the guild. This is an easy one to follow. Don't do it. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><u>Guild chat is not to be
     abused</u>. This includes spamming the the guild chat with senseless
     banter, and repeatedly sending messages to guild chat that are intended
     for your group or a private tell. Of course mistells happen and those are
     not a big deal. However, sending mistells to the guild chat on a somewhat
     regular basis is just sloppy and annoying. Our advice is to learn the
     /commands (/g - group, /gu - guild, etc). Changing your default channel
     using the EQ game interface is slow and often leads to mistells. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'><u>All members will follow
     all the rules of conduct of EQ</u>. This includes the play nice policies
     set forth by Verant, and not cheating or hacking EQ. <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<h3>Second chance, but not a third<o:p></o:p></h3>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:.5in;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
auto;margin-left:.5in'>If it has been determined that you have willfully
violated any of the rules, you will be contacted and issued a warning. If you
violate the same rule again, you will be disbanded from Bloodhorde. Hence, you
get a second chance but not a third. <o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal>Note that this does not apply to begging. The begging offense
is a one time deal. You do it, you are out.</p>

